    "result_text": "The full test suite consists solely of `AcceptanceTest` (the other files in that package are the `AcceptanceBase` harness and `AuditLogCapture` helper). Both tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the derived `ownerSegment` field on the Owner API response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`util/LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 added `ownerSegment(membershipLevel, customerCode, postcode, city)`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA = `METRO` when the derived locality (via the existing `forCustomerCode` region derivation) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`. Known-region membership is checked against the `REGION_POSTCODES` keys, reusing the module's single source of truth for regions.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` calling the new helper, matching the style of the existing `locality`/`timezone` mappings.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (with spec-matching description and example), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nVerified against the two acceptance tests: Sydney (NSW) owner at membership level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`; a random unknown-city owner \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`. Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
